{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun","id":804579,"title":"Gift of the Gun","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-09T11:41:25-08:00","id":804579,"title":"Gift of the Gun","content":"This was something I started thinking about when second edition first came out, then kept forgetting about and coming back to. I originally thought of it as part of a 'Lodge of the Silver Bullet,' which had a 'Gift of the Silver Bullet, then split into a Gift of Silver that sought some sort of overcoming of the werewolf's bane, and the Gift of the Gun. I hadn't really sat down and decided to write it down until today but some of the concepts I'd mulled over since the original idea. Since reading Acrozatarim's really helpful gift guides, I realize this probably doesn't exactly fit all the does and don'ts, it obviously places a lot of emphasis on ranged combat and I don't know if it 'absolutely nails the themes and symbolism' of the gun. Also the Purity one doesn't really fit what he described Purity gifts should aim for, and the fluff for it is awful. I'm still open to ideas, of course, which is why I'm posting it.<br /> <br /> The facets require a gun, which can be a revolver, pistol, rifle, and so forth, but not things like rocket launchers or crossbows.<br /> <br /> <b>Quietus (Cunning)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A drawback to the gun is the noise. While it can lead a hunter to their prey, it can also startle them away. This facet nullifies the roar of the werewolf's gun, and potentially goes further.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Stealth + Cunning<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> <i><b>Roll Results</b></i><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Firing the gun alerts everyone in the area to exactly where the shooter is and identifies them as the shooter.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The gun fires as normal.<br /> <b>Success:</b> From firing to impact, no flash is made and the bullets shot make no sound, even if firing into something that might make noise, like a bell. The only sound remaining is the bullet tearing through the air. Note that this doesn't silence the target, and screams or shattering after the impact may result.<br /> Spending a point of Essence per bullet fired takes the facet a step further, superficially 'sealing' glass and barriers the bullet has passed through. It will even close up skin the bullet has pierced, though it leaves wounds from the bullets passage through a body.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Uratha can gain the extra ability for free up to their Cunning in times during the duration of the facet.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Stopping Power (Glory)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">With this facet the Uratha focuses his soul through the fearful lens of the brandished gun.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> For the duration of the Facet, as long as the Uratha is openly wielding a gun, they gain the Primal Fear ability, as if in Gauru form. In addition, add the Uratha's Glory to any Down and Dirty rolls while using the gun.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>All Skill (Honor)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You've earned what you learned, and with this facet nothing is going to take that away from you.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> With this facet, all shooter-side penalties to firing a gun are reduced by the Honor of the character. This includes penalties for range, shooting offhand, dual-wielding as well as Environmental, but not Personal, Tilts and wound penalties. Modifiers from the target, including cover from both sides and possibly Defense, still remain, as do Specified Target shots.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Equalizer (Purity)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The gun exists to kill. Empowering this facet makes the gun equally lethal to all things.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> Activating this facet when firing allows an attack that hits a target to do lethal damage, even if the target would normally reduce that damage to bashing or less. The wounds created from this facet are painful and debilitating to anything that is self-aware.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Eye for Weakness (Wisdom)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This facet imbues a werewolf's gun with the spirit of the hunter within them, giving their bullets an inescapable hunger for prey.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Firearms + Wisdom<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> <i><b>Roll Results</b></i><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Uratha's bullets are especially poor at finding their target, not doing more than base weapon damage.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> There is no effect.<br /> <b>Success:</b> For the scene, bullets fired by the werewolf gain Armor Piercing equal to the werewolf's Wisdom.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> In addition to the success result, the bullets also gain twice the werewolf's Wisdom in regard to piercing Durability.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-09-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:46:32-08:00","id":804582,"title":"","content":"Well, this is great. I might suggest changing the name of the Wisdom Facet, not just because it's controversial, but also because it's a little clunky and Armor Piercing doesn't really resonate with that title. Until we start giving our kids armor, anyway.<br /> <br /> But otherwise I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:52:11-08:00","id":804588,"title":"","content":"I kinda wanna name the Wisdom Facet as &quot;Shots Fired!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:57:07-08:00","id":804593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=804582#post804582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is great. I might suggest changing the name of the Wisdom Facet, not just because it's controversial, but also because it's a little clunky and Armor Piercing doesn't really resonate with that title. Until we start giving our kids armor, anyway.<br /> <br /> But otherwise I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The name for the facet comes from a quote, from Johnny Dangerously, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hd-0F4v1C54\" target=\"_blank\">with a ridiculously over the top antagonist very fond of guns</a>. I'll find another name for it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:52:35-08:00","id":804640,"title":"","content":"Ah, then maybe it makes sense then. I don't really know the reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T13:27:41-08:00","id":804661,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=804588#post804588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wanna name the Wisdom Facet as &quot;Shots Fired!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I was thinking of the Glory one as 'Lone Gunman' or something that would play upon the fears revolving around guns, too.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=804640#post804640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, then maybe it makes sense then. I don't really know the reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an old movie, but funny. I changed it anyways. I was thinking, 'For Duck Hunting,' or 'Wolf Fang Bullet,' but for now just Eye for Weakness will suffice.<br /> <br /> I also changed the Purity facet, as it was bothering me. I figure if we're getting more accurate with the symbolism of the gun, it's not a protective thing except potentially in deterrence, it doesn't really block other bullets from you so a defensive facet was sort of sticking out odd. I think the replacement, Equalizer, is better. It's mainly for dealing with things like spirits, who reduce lethal to bashing. If a vampire fan has a problem with that, they can confine it to work on ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> Here is the original facet, just in case.<br /> <br /> Stainless Steel Wolf (Purity)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Like water off a duck's back, so are the bullets of the enemy.<br /> Cost: 1 Essence<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> A werewolf can activate this ability when a bullet has struck them. If the damage of the bullet, after armor is checked, does not exceed the werewolf's Purity, the bullet stops at the werewolf's flesh, unable to harm them.<br /> Some more flamboyant werewolves use this ability to 'catch' bullets.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:37:06-08:00","id":805025,"title":"","content":"Well, this is definitely THE Gift that makes firearms users <i>very</i> fierce hunters. I can definitely see this being a staple for Iron Masters and (to a lesser extent) Blood Talons.<br /> <br /> One thing I have to ask, though. Is Equalizer tailored for combating supernaturals like Vampires, Mages with Death Armor, and (1E) Sin-Eaters? Because if it does, I am curious enough to wonder if it can cause more devastating harm to regular mortals. Perhaps you can add something like..<br /> <br /> &quot;If a mortal is the target of a Firearms attack imbued with Equalizer, he upgrades an amount of damage equal to the werewolf's Purity Renown into Aggravated Damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or is that too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-10-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:01:32-08:00","id":805248,"title":"","content":"Very cool, and a good example of when it's okay to bend or break guidelines. This feels appropriate for the Forsaken and keeps them in your face, even if they are hunting at range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T14:10:43-08:00","id":805474,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=805025#post805025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I have to ask, though. Is Equalizer tailored for combating supernaturals like Vampires, Mages with Death Armor, and (1E) Sin-Eaters? Because if it does, I am curious enough to wonder if it can cause more devastating harm to regular mortals. Perhaps you can add something like..<br /> <br /> &quot;If a mortal is the target of a Firearms attack imbued with Equalizer, he upgrades an amount of damage equal to the werewolf's Purity Renown into Aggravated Damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or is that too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was designed for spirits, who normally reduce Lethal physical attacks to Bashing wounds, but as it's basically like the name says, an Equalizer, I think it would be fair to have it be used against others. It's all following old sayings like, 'God created man, Sam Colt made them equal,' and the idea that holding a gun gives you the power to kill another. Having it do extra damage would sort of go against that. That said, I really embrace the idea of using fetishes to alter weapons, so I would probably have a Manhunter fetish or something that amplifies the facet's ability like you said. But of course, if you wanted to use it for your games the way you want I wouldn't tell you otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-10-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:39:09-08:00","id":806071,"title":"","content":"If you want some feedback from me, I can go through the Gift and give it an analysis from the mechanics and thematics side of things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:47:02-08:00","id":806077,"title":"","content":"That would be wolftastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:34:08-08:00","id":806160,"title":"","content":"Alright!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quietus (Cunning)</b> </div> </div> </div> This Facet doesn't meaningfully scale in any way. It has Cunning in its dice pool, but passing the roll is trivial and isn't contested or resisted. It's better off being switched to a no-roll effect that involves Cunning scaling in some way, or that doesn't scale at all. Right now the rolled element is just increasing its complexity pointlessly.<br /> <br /> 'My gun is silenced' is a trivial effect and not worth a whole Facet. It's also too narrow to really make sense as 'the predator's reflected Cunning for firearms'.<br /> <br /> The second effect is far more interesting and I'd be more interested in seeing this Facet be all about the 'traceless killing' in general rather than its initial focus on sound and silence.<br /> <br /> The name is a bit goofy as well since I instantly think Assamite, which probably isn't what you should be looking for with a Forsaken Facet for firearms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Stopping Power (Glory)</b> </div> </div> </div> The 'adds Glory to Down and Dirty' bit of this is fine, even if it does feel rather close to Merciless Gunman or whatever the power is called from Demon.<br /> <br /> However, the general adding of Primal Fear rather than 'can down and dirty like Primal Fear' feels a bit odd. The only enemy that the other bit of Primal Fear actually helps against is other werewolves. That's not... really much of an issue, but I wonder what your overall intent was for adding the whole Primal Fear effect, as this may help understand what you're going for.<i>\u200b</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>All Skill (Honor)</b> </div> </div> </div> This seems fine although the name is a bit underwhelming. What's the reasoning behind not let it apply to personal Tilts and wound penalties?<br /> <br /> I still find myself thinking this isn't quite... gun-y enough, though. It's a skill-based benefit that happens to be with guns, not really something defining *about* being a predator with a gun, you know?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Equalizer (Purity)</b> </div> </div> </div> Eh. No Purity scaling at all and an extremely narrow effect. I'd suggest rolling the Wisdom Facet's effects into this one, giving both AP=Purity and ignoring supernatural lethal-&gt;bashing damage downgrades but at an increased cost in Essence (since Shield Breaker just adds AP to melee for 1 Essence per attack).<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I'd be tempted to make it something like Essence 3 and only be useable on an Aimed firearms attack, then roll in the effect to be something like Purity AP, goes *through* up to Purity in Durability of structure without meaningful damage (letting you pop shots through walls) and staying as Lethal even vs supernatural effects that would downgrade it. Make it the ultimate expression of the aimed killer shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Eye for Weakness (Wisdom)</b> </div> </div> </div> I have no idea why this is a rolled Facet. It's trivial to pass and already has Wisdom factored in as a scaling effect in adding the AP.<br /> <br /> I also note it's a scene long. Comparing to Shield Breaker, this should be 1 Essence per attack (if not more due to being a firearm), not 1 Essence per scene.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:44:28-08:00","id":806343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=806160#post806160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright!<br /> The more I think about it, the more I'd be tempted to make it something like Essence 3 and only be useable on an Aimed firearms attack, then roll in the effect to be something like Purity AP, goes *through* up to Purity in Durability of structure without meaningful damage (letting you pop shots through walls) and staying as Lethal even vs supernatural effects that would downgrade it. Make it the ultimate expression of the aimed killer shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please note, you can't actually aim at nothing thru say, walls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:32:05-08:00","id":806418,"title":"","content":"Okay, I got what you mean with Cunning. I figure the fluff probably needs work all around, too.<br /> <br /> The Primal Fear thing was a mistake on my part, I keep thinking it had the ability from the open development leak, where you needed to spend Willpower to attack them. But that's been changed so point taken.<br /> <br /> For Honor, yeah the name was bad. I was hesitant to let it add Personal tilts in concern it might be seen as too powerful, plus certain imagery about firing with some Personal tilts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=806160#post806160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. No Purity scaling at all and an extremely narrow effect. I'd suggest rolling the Wisdom Facet's effects into this one, giving both AP=Purity and ignoring supernatural lethal-&gt;bashing damage downgrades but at an increased cost in Essence (since Shield Breaker just adds AP to melee for 1 Essence per attack).<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I'd be tempted to make it something like Essence 3 and only be useable on an Aimed firearms attack, then roll in the effect to be something like Purity AP, goes *through* up to Purity in Durability of structure without meaningful damage (letting you pop shots through walls) and staying as Lethal even vs supernatural effects that would downgrade it. Make it the ultimate expression of the aimed killer shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I like that. I have to admit figuring out Essence costs was a toughie so I sort of retreated back to 1.<br /> <br /> Point taken about Wisdom, back to the drawing board.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot for the feedback, though, I really appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:12:45-08:00","id":806670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=806343#post806343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please note, you can't actually aim at nothing thru say, walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, wolf senses says that you ignore any blindness penalties so long as one of your senses applies, and wolf hearing applies within 1 mile per primal urge. So I would think that a werewolf with wolf senses active could probably aim relying purely on hearing rather easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:03:00-08:00","id":806775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=806670#post806670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, wolf senses says that you ignore any blindness penalties so long as one of your senses applies, and wolf hearing applies within 1 mile per primal urge. So I would think that a werewolf with wolf senses active could probably aim relying purely on hearing rather easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you'd think a gun-totting gift would actually rely on hand-eye coordination.<br /> <br /> I'd call that echo-location. Not aiming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:03:26-08:00","id":807058,"title":"","content":"My point is that for an Uratha, there isn't a lot of difference between hand eyes coordination, and ear eye coordination. So long as it helps you line up your shot, that's aiming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:17:22-08:00","id":807069,"title":"","content":"Maybe that could be the Wisdom Gift. Taking aim at people you can't really see.<br /> <br /> Or the Cunning one a sort of 'Twilight Bullet' that simply goes through things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:56:58-08:00","id":807103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/804579-gift-of-the-gun?p=807069#post807069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that could be the Wisdom Gift. Taking aim at people you can't really see.<br /> <br /> Or the Cunning one a sort of 'Twilight Bullet' that simply goes through things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It very much aligns with Wisdom giving aditional information or means to execute tasks. I could see a facet reducing cover penalties by Wisdom, like if while holding a gun, the Werewolf received another sense, the Aiming <i>per se. &quot;You can run but you can't hide&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> I agree with Wild-Eyes, Werewolf senses help mitigate eye penalties, so they should help aiming if the individual has trained for it. It is actually kind of like echolocation, a Daredevilish way to aim. Even &quot;smell-location&quot; should help somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}